  "title": "Passive vs Active Voice",
  "titleRussian": "Активный vs пассивный залог",
  "description": "Choosing voice for different styles",
  "descriptionRussian": "Выбор залога в зависимости от стиля",
  "imageName": "arrow.left.arrow.right",
  "intro": "Russian uses voice strategically for style and emphasis. ACTIVE preferred in: colloquial speech, direct narratives, when agent is important. PASSIVE preferred in: formal/official texts, scientific writing, when agent is unknown or unimportant. IMPERSONAL as alternative: Здесь не курят (general rule). KEY: Active feels personal and direct; passive feels objective and formal. Russian has more options than English: reflexive passive (строится), short participle (построен), impersonal (говорят).",
  "rules": [
    "Active for colloquial/personal: Мы решили эту проблему (We solved this problem)",
    "Passive for formal/objective: Проблема была решена (The problem was solved)",
    "Impersonal for general rules: Здесь не курят (No smoking here)",
    "Agent often omitted in passive: Статья написана (by whom = unimportant)"
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Active (direct): Комиссия рассмотрела заявку. (The committee reviewed the application.)",
    "Passive (formal): Заявка была рассмотрена. (The application was reviewed.)",
    "Reflexive passive: Документы рассматриваются. (Documents are being reviewed.)",
    "Impersonal: В институте изучают русский. (Russian is studied at the institute.)"
  ],
